    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "R1",
        "severity": "HIGH",
        "location": "ledger.py:9-10,20-23,26-38",
        "requirement": "Validate integer values, reject invalid transfers with ValueError without changing state, and preserve transfer and replay integrity.",
        "evidence": "Scalar subclasses pass isinstance checks and retain overridden behavior. Reproducer:\nfrom ledger import Ledger\nclass NegativeAmount(int):\n    def __le__(self, other): return False\nledger = Ledger({'a': 10, 'b': 0})\nledger.transfer('a', 'b', NegativeAmount(-1), 'x')\nObserved: success, balances {'a': 11, 'b': -1}, and history records amount -1. Separate probes of this same scalar-handling flaw demonstrated creation of funds through overridden arithmetic, acceptance of changed replay amounts through overridden equality, and a str subclass causing ValueError after balances changed but before history was recorded.",
        "suggested_fix": "Normalize accepted scalar subclasses to trusted built-in values before validation, arithmetic, hashing, comparison and storage. Add focused tests covering these boundaries and failure atomicity."
      },
      {
        "id": "R2",
        "severity": "LOW",
        "location": "ledger.py:49,56",
        "requirement": "Malformed batch operations must be rejected with ValueError without changing state.",
        "evidence": "Reproducer:\nfrom collections import UserString\nfrom ledger import Ledger\nledger = Ledger({'a': 10, 'b': 0})\nledger.batch([{UserString('source'): 'a', 'target': 'b', 'amount': 1, 'key': 'x'}])\nObserved: TypeError('keywords must be strings'), rather than ValueError. UserString('source') passes the field-set equality check despite not being a str. State remained unchanged, including when a valid operation preceded this malformed operation.",
        "suggested_fix": "Validate field-name types alongside the exact required names before expanding operation dictionaries into keyword arguments."
      }
    ],
    "checks": [
      "Read lean-run, CONTRACT.md and AGENTS.md; reviewed the complete baseline-to-candidate source diff and all added tests.",
      "Confirmed supplied test_public.py matches its baseline.",
      "python3 -B -m unittest discover -v: all 22 tests passed on Python 3.14.3.",
      "Independent temporary-script integrated flow passed: ordinary subclasses, dependent transfers, replay, receipt isolation, dictionary identity and failed-batch rollback.",
      "Independent probes reproduced both findings and the related scalar-integrity failures described above.",
      "Verified application, tests, instructions and baseline hashes remained unchanged; temporary probe files were removed."
    ],
    "coverage_limits": [
      "Scalar-integrity failures require custom Python subclasses; no remote-input path exists in this fixture.",
      "Assessment covered the single-process, in-memory contract on the available Python runtime; arbitrary subclass behaviors and resource-exhaustion failures were not exhaustively tested."
    ]
